---
title: Writing a page
description: Where pages live, and how the sidebar finds them.
---

Every page is a Markdown file under `docs/src/content/docs/`. Its path is its
address: `guides/writing-a-page.md` is served at `/{{ repo_name }}/guides/writing-a-page/`.

A page placed in `guides/` or `reference/` appears in the sidebar by itself.
A new directory needs one line in the `sidebar` of `astro.config.mjs`.

Links between pages start from the site's base, `/{{ repo_name }}/`. The build
checks every one of them, so a link written from the root fails the build
instead of shipping a broken page.

Replace this page with the first guide the product needs.
